    "result_text": "All 290 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created, the application now counts how many existing owners share the same last name at that moment and returns it as the integer field `namesakeCount` in the owner response.\n\nFollowing the established pattern for the other creation-time computed fields (`membershipNumber`, `customerCode`, `membershipTier`), I made these changes:\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 computes the count via a new `countNamesakes(lastName)` helper (streams existing owners, matching last name exactly, excluding the not-yet-persisted new owner) and sets it on the owner before saving.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `namesakeCount` field (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `namesakeCount` property to the `Owner` schema (readOnly int32, min 0), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n- **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`** \u2014 added two tests: `0` for a unique last name, and `1`/`2` as owners accumulate under the same last name.\n\nVerified: `290 tests run, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS`.",
